  "answer": "Project Zenith is a new data analytics and AI initiative aimed at revolutionizing the company's approach to data. It was introduced by Alex with a kick-off on June 15th and a Phase One budget of $500,000, led by Sarah Tan. The project has seen significant progress, including initial findings of a potential 20% efficiency increase (reported by Tom on August 5th) and a breakthrough in predictive analytics (reported by Neil on November 20th). The team has expanded to include new members specializing in cybersecurity, cloud architecture, machine learning, and cloud computing, with onboarding sessions scheduled for September 10th. Key milestones include the successful testing of a secure file sharing prototype ahead of schedule, with UI enhancements planned for October. The project also involves exploring partnerships with TechInnovate for AI technology and has increased its compliance plan budget to $55,000. Feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience is being sought by the end of November."
